# Build context for every Dockerfile stage (base, dev, test). The Dockerfile COPYs
# `app/` (base) and `tests/` (dev/test stages) explicitly, so exclude everything that
# must never enter an image or would bust the build cache.

# Git
.git
.gitignore

# Python / caches. `**/` because a bare pattern matches only at the context root, and
# `COPY app /app/app` would otherwise bake the host's gitignored app/**/__pycache__ into a
# release (2026.10.1 shipped July-dated .pyc files and a .DS_Store that way).
**/__pycache__
**/*.py[cod]
**/*.so
.Python
.venv
venv/
env/
ENV/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.pytest_cache/
.coverage
htmlcov/

# Secrets / env — must NEVER enter the image (only .env.example is harmless)
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Runtime output + quarantined captures (bind-mounted / local-only, never baked)
output/
export/
json/

# Docs / dashboards (not needed in the runtime image)
docs/
grafana/
*.md

# Compose / Dockerfiles / build tooling
compose*.yaml
compose*.yml
Dockerfile*
Makefile

# OS / editor
**/.DS_Store
**/Thumbs.db
**/*.swp
.vscode/
.idea/

# Claude
.claude/
